<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lindanise</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1219">1219</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Valdemar · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-crusade">Livonian Crusade</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lindanise was fought on 15 June 1219 at the site of present-day Tallinn, when the crusading army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a> of Rävala. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> then built a castle on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toompea">Toompea</a>, around which the town of Reval grew. Legend holds that the Danish flag, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flag-of-denmark">Dannebrog</a>, fell from the sky during the battle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lindanise.jpg" alt="Battle of Lindanise" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian August Lorentzen · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danmarks_flag_1219_Lorentzen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
